{"id":"chatcmpl-f2221b81-0cad-4d05-a89b-abe96ecaef64","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244440,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a binary laterality question (left vs. right) about a localized radiographic finding. The successful strategy combines an expert interpretation tool with independent visual grounding tools to cross-verify the side of the abnormality. The key insight is triangulating multiple evidence sources (expert description, grounded report, phrase grounding) to confirm laterality before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When options differ only by laterality (left vs. right), explicitly query for the side/location rather than the general finding.\",\n    \"Use an expert interpretation tool first to get a directional hypothesis, then verify with independent grounding tools to avoid single-source error.\",\n    \"Cross-check the hypothesized side using phrase grounding against image coordinates to confirm the finding maps to the correct anatomical region.\",\n    \"Resolve binary anatomical questions by triangulating multiple independent evidence sources before selecting the answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Radiology multiple-choice\": \"Ask location-specific questions to disambiguate laterality; confirm with coordinate-based grounding before answering.\",\n    \"Binary visual discrimination\": \"Convert the choice into a directional/locational query, then verify with a second independent method.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted diagnosis\": \"Chain an expert-description tool with a grounding tool so each validates the other's claim.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding's laterality matches the image coordinate region (e.g., right side maps to expected x-range on frontal view).\",\n    \"Ensure at least two independent tools agree on the side before finalizing the answer.\"\n 